<%# locals: (folder:, messages: nil, selected_id: nil, streams: []) %>
<%#
  The conversation list's frame. With `messages` it holds the folder's rows (the
  index, and MessagesConcern#index's answer to this frame's own request). With
  none it is the thread page's lazy frame: Turbo fetches its src only once the
  frame is on screen, which the list column never is below lg, so a phone
  opening a thread never loads the folder. refresh: morph reloads it after a
  morphing page refresh, which would otherwise leave the placeholder behind.
  Either way it lists a search's hits instead while there is one (?q=, ?with[]=).

  `streams` ride inside the frame's own answer and run as it renders: the tab
  row, which a search takes away (MessagesConcern#index).
%>
<% if messages %>
  <%= turbo_frame_tag "messages-conversation-list" do %>
    <%= render partial: "common/messages/conversation_list", locals: { messages:, folder:, selected_id: } %>
    <%= safe_join(streams) %>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <%= turbo_frame_tag "messages-conversation-list", src: messages_path(folder:, selected: selected_id, **search_scope),
                                                    loading: :lazy, refresh: :morph do %>
    <%= render "shared/frame_spinner", label: "Loading conversations…" %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
